Assignment 4 – Repository with at Least Three Meaningful Commits

Objective

To understand Git repository creation, version control, and the importance of meaningful commit messages.

1. Git Identity Setup

Before making commits, configure the Git username and email.

git config --global user.name "Your Name"
git config --global user.email "you@example.com"

Replace the example values with your own Git name and email.

2. Create a Repository

mkdir html-css-assignments
cd html-css-assignments
git init
git branch -M main

These commands create a project folder, initialize a Git repository, and set the main branch.

3. Commit 1 – Add README

echo "# HTML & CSS Assignments" > README.md
git add README.md
git commit -m "docs: add README with project overview"

Purpose: Add an introductory README file to the repository.

4. Commit 2 – Add Setup and Git Assignments

git add 01-*.md 02-*.md 03-*.md 04-*.md 05-*.md
git commit -m "docs: add setup and git assignments (1-5)"

Purpose: Add the documentation files for the first five assignments.

5. Commit 3 – Add HTML Basics

git add 06-*.html 07-*.html 08-*.html 09-*.html 10-*.html
git commit -m "feat: add HTML basics assignments (6-10)"

Purpose: Track the HTML assignment files in Git.

Note: These commands assume the corresponding files already exist in the repository. The file patterns may need to be adjusted to match the actual filenames.

6. Verify Commit History

git log --oneline

This command displays the commit history in a concise format.

7. Good Commit Message Rules

1. Use clear, action-oriented wording.
2. Add a type prefix such as "feat:", "fix:", "docs:", or "style:".
3. Keep each commit focused on one logical change.
4. Describe the change accurately.

8. Suggested Commit History for the Course

Commit| Message
1| "docs: add README"
2| "docs: setup and git assignments (1-5)"
3| "feat: add HTML basics (6-10)"
4| "feat: add links, images, and lists (11-15)"
5| "feat: add forms, tables, and metadata (16-20)"
6| "style: add CSS fundamentals (21-25)"
7| "style: add box model and positioning (26-30)"
8| "feat: add flexbox layouts (31-35)"
9| "feat: add grid layouts (36-40)"
10| "feat: add responsive landing page (41-45)"

Conclusion

Git helps developers track project changes and maintain a clear history of their work. Meaningful commits make projects easier to understand, review, and maintain.